 ongoing operations adjusted free cash flow before growth, as set forth on slide six.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"VST 2020 Q3","e":"vst","d":"2020-11-04","l":"guidance","r":"management","s":"Scott Hudson","x":"And we are currently on track to exceed our recently raised 2020 guidance midpoint of $955 million, with our 2021 adjusted EBITDA projected at nearly $1 billion.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"VST 2020 Q3","e":"vst","d":"2020-11-04","l":"guidance","r":"analyst","s":"Curt Morgan","x":"Today, we are reaffirming our recently raised 2020 guidance ranges as set forth on Slide 6.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"VST 2020 Q4","e":"vst","d":"2021-02-26","l":"pricing_power","r":"analyst","s":"Curtis Morgan","x":"And I think they are asking themselves, and they know the answer, none of them can stomach really the idea that a bunch of this high pricing power is going to get passed on to customers.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"VST 2020 Q4","e":"vst","d":"2021-02-26","l":"cost_cuts","r":"analyst","s":"Curtis Morgan","x":"We continue on the cost savings front.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"VST 2020 Q4","e":"vst","d":"2021-02-26","l":"cost_cuts","r":"analyst","s":"Curtis Morgan","x":"And some people may say, \"Well, there is a cost savings right there, Curt, why did you do that?","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"VST 2021 Q2","e":"vst","d":"2021-08-05","l":"guidance","r":"analyst","s":"Curt Morgan","x":"As a result, we are reaffirming our 2021 guidance ranges for both ongoing operations adjusted EBITDA and ongoing operations adjusted free cash flow before growth as set forth on Slide 6.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"VST 2021 Q4","e":"vst","d":"2022-02-25","l":"guidance","r":"analyst","s":"Curt Morgan","x":"Today, we are also reaffirming our 2022 guidance.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"VST 2022 Q4","e":"vst","d":"2023-03-01","l":"pricing_power","r":"analyst","s":"Jim Burke","x":"And what we've done in Texas, as you know, is we slowed down some of the merchant solar development because we've seen those returns be challenged based on not only EPC cost and panel costs, but solar is already starting to cannibalize solar in terms of price realization.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"VST 2022 Q4","e":"vst","d":"2023-03-01","l":"guidance","r":"management","s":"Kris Moldovan","x":"As Jim mentioned earlier, we are reaffirming our guidance for ongoing operations adjusted EBITDA with a $3.7 billion midpoint for 2023.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"VST 2023 Q3","e":"vst","d":"2023-11-07","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Scott Hudson","x":"…larger sophisticated customers want to work with players of scale, because we can structure a lot of complex products whether those be indexed, fixed, stability and pass through, new charges in the ERCOT markets, we see a shift of customers to the larger players in this particular environment.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"VST 2023 Q3","e":"vst","d":"2023-11-07","l":"cost_cuts","r":"analyst","s":"Jim Burke","x":"We don't have all the details on the Energy Harbor cost per -- I know they reset some of theirs early on as they did their restructuring, but we could have some exposure towards the back-end of a five-year planning horizon on price, just because the curves have moved up.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"VST 2024 Q1","e":"vst","d":"2024-05-08","l":"streaming","r":"management","s":"Scott Hudson","x":"We grew residential direct-to-consumer customer counts by 13%.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"VST 2024 Q2","e":"vst","d":"2024-08-08","l":"pricing_power","r":"analyst","s":"Jim Burke","x":"So you wouldn't expect that to pass-through at the full value.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"VST 2024 Q2","e":"vst","d":"2024-08-08","l":"pricing_power","r":"analyst","s":"Jim Burke","x":"Some of the commercial industrial contracts would pass-through.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"VST 2024 Q2","e":"vst","d":"2024-08-08","l":"guidance","r":"analyst","s":"Jim Burke","x":"We are reaffirming our guidance range for 2024 ongoing operations adjusted EBITDA of $4.550 billion to $5.050 billion.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"VST 2024 Q3","e":"vst","d":"2024-11-07","l":"guidance","r":"analyst","s":"Jim Burke","x":"For these reasons, we are maintaining our outlook for our 2026 ongoing operations adjusted EBITDA midpoint opportunity of over $6 billion with line of sight to potentially be meaningfully higher.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"VST 2024 Q4","e":"vst","d":"2025-02-27","l":"ai_spend","r":"analyst","s":"Jim Burke","x":"Importantly, the source of this expected load growth remains diversified across industries, with power demand related to AI data centers being only one aspect of the growth in large load sources.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"VST 2024 Q4","e":"vst","d":"2025-02-27","l":"ai_spend","r":"analyst","s":"Jim Burke","x":"As we've discussed on previous calls, we expect load growth to come from many sources, including residential, onshoring and manufacturing, oil and gas electrification, as well as data centers, including those focused on AI.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"VST 2024 Q4","e":"vst","d":"2025-02-27","l":"guidance","r":"management","s":"Kris Moldovan","x":"As for the curves, I think you'll see that historically as we reaffirmed guidance, we haven't updated the know, we say that it's still based on the curves because we're reaffirming the guidance that we gave before.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"VST 2024 Q4","e":"vst","d":"2025-02-27","l":"guidance","r":"analyst","s":"Jim Burke","x":"Moving to our longer-term outlook, we are reaffirming our guidance of $5.5 billion to $6.1 billion in adjusted free cash flow before growth of $3 billion to $3.6 billion that were introduced on our third quarter call.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"VST 2025 Q1","e":"vst","d":"2025-05-07","l":"tariffs","r":"analyst","s":"Jim Burke","x":"Importantly, cost structures for these projects remain insulated from recently announced tariffs.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"VST 2025 Q1","e":"vst","d":"2025-05-07","l":"tariffs","r":"analyst","s":"Jim Burke","x":"They said they were open to them, as we all would be, if settlement discussions are ordered, but their position is that no changes are needed to the tariff.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"VST 2025 Q1","e":"vst","d":"2025-05-07","l":"guidance","r":"management","s":"Kristopher Moldovan","x":"We believe the reaffirmed outlook for 2025 demonstrates the earnings resiliency afforded by the diversified model especially in light of our outage at Martin Lake Unit 1 and our MOS landing batteries being offline.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"VST 2025 Q1","e":"vst","d":"2025-05-07","l":"guidance","r":"analyst","s":"Jim Burke","x":"We are reaffirming the guidance ranges for 2025 adjusted EBITDA of $5.5 billion to $6.1 billion and a